From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:55:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] pinctrl: aw9523: Leave the interrupt trigger to the
 consumer

The driver gives its irqchip a default trigger of both edges. gpiolib
refuses a default trigger on a chip described by firmware, since the
consumer's description sets the trigger, and warns on every probe:

  /soc/i2c@1101a000/gpio@5b: Ignoring 3 default trigger
  WARNING: drivers/gpio/gpiolib.c:2107 at gpiochip_add_irqchip+0x4e4/0x500

Set no default. gpiolib already replaced the default with none, so the
interrupts behave as before; consumers asking for both edges still get
them through irq_set_type().

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c
index 02a24ac..5ccacef 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c
@@ -824,7 +824,7 @@ static int aw9523_init_irq(struct aw9523 *awi, int irq)
 	girq->parent_handler = NULL;
 	girq->num_parents = 0;
 	girq->parents = NULL;
-	girq->default_type = IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH;
+	girq->default_type = IRQ_TYPE_NONE;
 	girq->handler = handle_simple_irq;
 	girq->threaded = true;
 
